IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa3-part8-subsidiary.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 8, Chapter 4 (Prohibition on subsidiary being
-- member of its holding company): ss 136 to 144; lines 1786-1878 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. See coa3-part8-members.l4 for how to read JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING.
--
-- SEAMS taken as INPUTS (PLAN.md section 4.1): s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company (MAYBE BOOLEAN);
-- s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme (MAYBE BOOLEAN); s 1173(1) UK regulated market (MAYBE BOOLEAN).
-- BORROWED TERMS (an Act outside the sources): s 1122 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010 ("connected"), ss 235 and 237(2) of
-- the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 ("collective investment scheme", "trustee", "the operator"), section 57 and
-- Part 3 of the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993, the Companies Act 1985 and the Companies (Northern Ireland)
-- Order 1986. Each is a MAYBE BOOLEAN or a plain fact the person states; NOTHING passes through as NOTHING.

-- ---- s 136: the prohibition ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 136(2) provision of this Chapter` IS ONE OF
    `s 136(2) section 138 (subsidiary acting as personal representative or trustee)`
    `s 136(2) section 141 (subsidiary acting as authorised dealer in securities)`
    `s 136(2) another provision of this Chapter`

-- src:1792 | (2) The exceptions are provided for in—
-- src:1793 | section 138 (subsidiary acting as personal representative or trustee), and
-- src:1794 | section 141 (subsidiary acting as authorised dealer in securities).
@ref s 136(2) The exceptions (src:1792-1794)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 136(2) provision of this Chapter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(2) the exception is provided for in the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 136(2) section 138 (subsidiary acting as personal representative or trustee)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 136(2) section 141 (subsidiary acting as authorised dealer in securities)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 136(2) another provision of this Chapter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The exceptions are provided for in— section 138 ..., and section 141" names two sections; s 137 also lets a body corporate continue as a member (fork F13)

-- "Except as provided by this Chapter": the three answers that provide for an exception are inputs, each the answer of
-- the section that gives it: s 137(1) (continue as a member), s 138(1) and s 141(1) (the prohibition does not apply).
-- src:1788 | 136 Prohibition on subsidiary being a member of its holding company
-- src:1789 | (1) Except as provided by this Chapter—
-- src:1790 | (a) a body corporate cannot be a member of a company that is its holding company, and
-- src:1791 | (b) any allotment or transfer of shares in a company to its subsidiary is void.
@ref s 136(1)(a) A body corporate cannot be a member of a company that is its holding company (src:1788-1791)
GIVEN `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 137(1) the body corporate may continue to be a member of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 138(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 141(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(1)(a) the prohibition applies: the body corporate cannot be a member of the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a body corporate cannot be a member of a company that is its holding company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1159(1) decides "subsidiary" and "holding company"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF       `s 137(1) the body corporate may continue to be a member of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR  `s 138(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR  `s 141(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as provided by this Chapter" (ss 137(1), 138(1), 141(1))
        ELSE IF       `s 137(1) the body corporate may continue to be a member of the company` EQUALS NOTHING
                  OR  `s 138(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` EQUALS NOTHING
                  OR  `s 141(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` EQUALS NOTHING
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an exception of this Chapter has not been decided
             ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 136(1)(b) An allotment or transfer of shares to the company's subsidiary is void (src:1788 and src:1791)
GIVEN `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 138(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 141(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(1)(b) the allotment or transfer of shares in the company to its subsidiary is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any allotment or transfer of shares in a company to its subsidiary is void"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1159(1) decides "subsidiary"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF       `s 138(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR  `s 141(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as provided by this Chapter" (ss 138(1), 141(1))
        ELSE IF       `s 138(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` EQUALS NOTHING
                  OR  `s 141(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` EQUALS NOTHING
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an exception of this Chapter has not been decided
             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 137: shares acquired before the prohibition became applicable ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1801 | (2) The relevant date for the purposes of subsection (1)(a) is—
-- src:1802 | (a) 1st July 1948 in the case of a company registered in Great Britain, and
-- src:1803 | (b) 1st April 1961 in the case of a company registered in Northern Ireland.
@ref s 137(2) The relevant date (src:1801-1803)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 137(2) the relevant date for the purposes of s 137(1)(a)` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN Date 1 4 1961
    OTHERWISE Date 1 7 1948 -- "Great Britain" is England and Wales together with Scotland

-- The commencement of this Chapter is a date outside the Act's own text, so it is an input. The limbs (b) and (c)
-- turn on whether an earlier prohibition (section 23(1) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 33(1) of the Companies
-- (Northern Ireland) Order 1986), or the prohibition in s 136, applied in the circumstances: facts the person states.
-- src:1795 | 137 Shares acquired before prohibition became applicable
-- src:1796 | (1) Where a body corporate became a holder of shares in a company—
-- src:1797 | (a) before the relevant date, or
-- src:1798 | (b) on or after that date and before the commencement of this Chapter in circumstances in which the prohibition in section 23(1) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 33(1) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6)) (or any corresponding earlier enactment), as it then had effect, did not apply, or
-- src:1799 | (c) on or after the commencement of this Chapter in circumstances in which the prohibition in section 136 did not apply,
-- src:1800 | it may continue to be a member of the company.
@ref s 137(1) A body corporate that became a holder of shares before the prohibition applied may continue to be a member (src:1795-1800)
GIVEN `the relevant date (s 137(2))` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the body corporate became a holder of shares in the company` IS A DATE
      `the date of the commencement of this Chapter` IS A DATE
      `the earlier prohibition did not apply in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prohibition in section 136 did not apply in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(1) the body corporate may continue to be a member of the company` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the body corporate became a holder of shares in the company` LESS THAN `the relevant date (s 137(2))`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- limb (a): "before the relevant date"
    ELSE IF `the date on which the body corporate became a holder of shares in the company` LESS THAN `the date of the commencement of this Chapter`
         THEN IF `the earlier prohibition did not apply in the circumstances`
              THEN JUST TRUE -- limb (b): "on or after that date and before the commencement of this Chapter in circumstances in which the prohibition ... did not apply"
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a body corporate became a holder of shares in a company ... in circumstances in which the prohibition in section 23(1) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 33(1) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 ... did not apply" (the "where" does not hold)
         ELSE IF `the prohibition in section 136 did not apply in the circumstances`
              THEN JUST TRUE -- limb (c): "on or after the commencement of this Chapter in circumstances in which the prohibition in section 136 did not apply"
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a body corporate became a holder of shares in a company ... on or after the commencement of this Chapter in circumstances in which the prohibition in section 136 did not apply" (the "where" does not hold)

-- src:1804 | (3) So long as it is permitted to continue as a member of a company by virtue of this section, an allotment to it of fully paid shares in the company may be validly made by way of capitalisation of reserves of the company.
@ref s 137(3) Allotment of fully paid shares by capitalisation of reserves (src:1804)
GIVEN `s 137(1) the body corporate is permitted to continue as a member of the company by virtue of s 137` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the shares allotted are fully paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is made by way of capitalisation of reserves of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(3) an allotment to the body corporate of fully paid shares in the company may be validly made by way of capitalisation of reserves` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 137(1) the body corporate is permitted to continue as a member of the company by virtue of s 137`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "So long as it is permitted to continue as a member of a company by virtue of this section"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 137(1) has not been decided
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the shares allotted are fully paid` AND `the allotment is made by way of capitalisation of reserves of the company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an allotment to it of fully paid shares in the company may be validly made by way of capitalisation of reserves of the company"

-- src:1805 | (4) But, so long as the prohibition in section 136 would (apart from this section) apply, it has no right to vote in respect of the shares mentioned in subsection (1) above, or any shares allotted as mentioned in subsection (3) above, on a written resolution or at meetings of the company or of any class of its members.
@ref s 137(4) No right to vote while the prohibition would apply (src:1805)
GIVEN `the prohibition in section 136 would (apart from section 137) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are mentioned in s 137(1) or were allotted as mentioned in s 137(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vote is on a written resolution or at a meeting of the company or of a class of its members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(4) the body corporate has a right to vote in respect of the shares` MEANS
    IF `the prohibition in section 136 would (apart from section 137) apply` AND `the shares are mentioned in s 137(1) or were allotted as mentioned in s 137(3)` AND `the vote is on a written resolution or at a meeting of the company or of a class of its members`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so long as the prohibition in section 136 would (apart from this section) apply, it has no right to vote in respect of the shares mentioned in subsection (1) above, or any shares allotted as mentioned in subsection (3) above, on a written resolution or at meetings of the company or of any class of its members"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence says there is no right to vote only so long as the prohibition would apply, and says nothing of a right to vote otherwise

-- ---- s 138: subsidiary acting as personal representative or trustee ------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1807 | 138 Subsidiary acting as personal representative or trustee
-- src:1808 | (1) The prohibition in section 136 (prohibition on subsidiary being a member of its holding company) does not apply where the subsidiary is concerned only—
-- src:1809 | (a) as personal representative, or
-- src:1810 | (b) as trustee,
-- src:1811 | unless, in the latter case, the holding company or a subsidiary of it is beneficially interested under the trust.
@ref s 138(1) The prohibition does not apply where the subsidiary is concerned only as personal representative or trustee (src:1807-1811)
GIVEN `the subsidiary is concerned only as personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary is concerned only as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holding company or a subsidiary of it is beneficially interested under the trust, disregarding the interests listed in s 138(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` MEANS
    IF `the subsidiary is concerned only as personal representative`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the subsidiary is concerned only as trustee`
         THEN IF `the holding company or a subsidiary of it is beneficially interested under the trust, disregarding the interests listed in s 138(2)`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless, in the latter case, the holding company or a subsidiary of it is beneficially interested under the trust"
              ELSE JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply where the subsidiary is concerned only— (a) as personal representative, or (b) as trustee"

DECLARE `s 138(2) interest` IS ONE OF
    `s 138(2)(a) an interest held by way of security` HAS
        `s 138(2)(a) held only by way of security` IS A BOOLEAN
        `s 138(2)(a) for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 138(2)(b)(i) an interest within section 139`
    `s 138(2)(b)(ii) an interest within section 140`
    `s 138(2)(c)(i) a right to recover expenses or be remunerated out of the trust property`
    `s 138(2)(c)(ii) a right to be indemnified out of the trust property for a liability incurred by reason of an act or omission in the performance of duties as trustee`
    `s 138(2) another interest`

-- src:1812 | (2) For the purpose of ascertaining whether the holding company or a subsidiary is so interested, there shall be disregarded—
-- src:1813 | (a) any interest held only by way of security for the purposes of a transaction entered into by the holding company or subsidiary in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money;
-- src:1814 | (b) any interest within—
-- src:1815 | section 139 (interests to be disregarded: residual interest under pension scheme or employees' share scheme), or
-- src:1816 | section 140 (interests to be disregarded: employer's rights of recovery under pension scheme or employees' share scheme);
-- src:1817 | (c) any rights that the company or subsidiary has in its capacity as trustee, including in particular—
-- src:1818 | (i) any right to recover its expenses or be remunerated out of the trust property, and
-- src:1819 | (ii) any right to be indemnified out of the trust property for any liability incurred by reason of any act or omission in the performance of its duties as trustee.
@ref s 138(2) Interests to be disregarded (src:1812-1819)
GIVEN interest IS A `s 138(2) interest`
      `s 139(1) the interest is disregarded for the purposes of s 138` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 140 the interest is disregarded for the purposes of s 138` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(2) the interest is disregarded in ascertaining whether the holding company or a subsidiary is beneficially interested` MEANS
    CONSIDER interest
    WHEN `s 138(2)(a) an interest held by way of security` a b THEN
        IF a AND b
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any interest held only by way of security for the purposes of a transaction entered into ... in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money"
    WHEN `s 138(2)(b)(i) an interest within section 139` THEN `s 139(1) the interest is disregarded for the purposes of s 138`
    WHEN `s 138(2)(b)(ii) an interest within section 140` THEN `s 140 the interest is disregarded for the purposes of s 138`
    WHEN `s 138(2)(c)(i) a right to recover expenses or be remunerated out of the trust property` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 138(2)(c)(ii) a right to be indemnified out of the trust property for a liability incurred by reason of an act or omission in the performance of duties as trustee` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 138(2) another interest` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists interests to be disregarded without closing the list ("there shall be disregarded ... (c) any rights ..., including in particular")

-- ---- s 139 and s 140: interests under a pension scheme or an employees' share scheme -----------------------------------------------------------

-- gloss: a "pension scheme" is a scheme that provides, or includes, pension-type benefits for employees or former employees.
-- src:1832 | (5) In this section “pension scheme” means a scheme for the provision of benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits for or in respect of employees or former employees.
@ref s 139(5) "pension scheme" (src:1832)
GIVEN `the scheme provides benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits for or in respect of employees or former employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(5) the scheme is a pension scheme` MEANS
    IF `the scheme provides benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits for or in respect of employees or former employees`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“pension scheme” means a scheme for the provision of benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits for or in respect of employees or former employees"

-- src:1820 | 139 Interests to be disregarded: residual interest under pension scheme or employees' share scheme
-- src:1821 | (1) Where shares in a company are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme, there shall be disregarded for the purposes of section 138 any residual interest that has not vested in possession.
@ref s 139(1) A residual interest that has not vested in possession is disregarded (src:1820-1821)
GIVEN `s 139(1) the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the interest is a residual interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest has vested in possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(1) the interest is disregarded for the purposes of s 138` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 139(1) the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares in a company are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1166 decides "employees' share scheme"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the interest is a residual interest` AND (NOT `the interest has vested in possession`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any residual interest that has not vested in possession"

-- the trust is for the purposes of a pension scheme or an employees' share scheme (a three-valued "or")
@ref s 139(1) Shares held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme (src:1820-1821)
GIVEN `shares in a company are held on trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 139(5) the scheme is a pension scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(1) the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme` MEANS
    IF NOT `shares in a company are held on trust`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares in a company are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme"
    ELSE IF `s 139(5) the scheme is a pension scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `s 139(5) the scheme is a pension scheme` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme"
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1166 decides "employees' share scheme"

-- src:1822 | (2) A “residual interest” means a right of the company or subsidiary (“the residual beneficiary”) to receive any of the trust property in the event of—
-- src:1823 | (a) all the liabilities arising under the scheme having been satisfied or provided for, or
-- src:1824 | (b) the residual beneficiary ceasing to participate in the scheme, or
-- src:1825 | (c) the trust property at any time exceeding what is necessary for satisfying the liabilities arising or expected to arise under the scheme.
@ref s 139(2) "residual interest" (src:1822-1825)
GIVEN `the right is a right of the company or subsidiary to receive any of the trust property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the event of all the liabilities arising under the scheme having been satisfied or provided for` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the event of the residual beneficiary ceasing to participate in the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the event of the trust property at any time exceeding what is necessary for satisfying the liabilities arising or expected to arise under the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(2) the right is a residual interest` MEANS
    IF       `the right is a right of the company or subsidiary to receive any of the trust property`
         AND (    `in the event of all the liabilities arising under the scheme having been satisfied or provided for`
              OR  `in the event of the residual beneficiary ceasing to participate in the scheme`
              OR  `in the event of the trust property at any time exceeding what is necessary for satisfying the liabilities arising or expected to arise under the scheme`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “residual interest” means a right of the company or subsidiary (“the residual beneficiary”) to receive any of the trust property in the event of— (a) ..., or (b) ..., or (c) ..."

-- src:1826 | (3) In subsection (2)—
-- src:1827 | (a) the reference to a right includes a right dependent on the exercise of a discretion vested by the scheme in the trustee or another person, and
@ref s 139(3)(a) A right includes a right dependent on a discretion (src:1826-1827)
GIVEN `the right depends on the exercise of a discretion vested by the scheme in the trustee or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(3)(a) the right is a right for the purposes of s 139(2)` MEANS
    IF `the right depends on the exercise of a discretion vested by the scheme in the trustee or another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to a right includes a right dependent on the exercise of a discretion" (an inclusive definition says nothing of other rights)

-- src:1826 | (3) In subsection (2)—
-- src:1828 | (b) the reference to liabilities arising under a scheme includes liabilities that have resulted, or may result, from the exercise of any such discretion.
@ref s 139(3)(b) Liabilities include liabilities resulting from a discretion (src:1826 and src:1828)
GIVEN `the liability has resulted, or may result, from the exercise of a discretion vested by the scheme in the trustee or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(3)(b) the liability is a liability arising under the scheme for the purposes of s 139(2)` MEANS
    IF `the liability has resulted, or may result, from the exercise of a discretion vested by the scheme in the trustee or another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to liabilities arising under a scheme includes liabilities that have resulted, or may result, from the exercise of any such discretion"

DECLARE `s 139(4) case of a residual interest` IS ONE OF
    `s 139(4)(a) a case within subsection (2)(a)`
    `s 139(4)(b) a case within subsection (2)(b) or (c)`

-- src:1829 | (4) For the purposes of this section a residual interest vests in possession—
-- src:1830 | (a) in a case within subsection (2)(a), on the occurrence of the event mentioned there (whether or not the amount of the property receivable pursuant to the right is ascertained);
-- src:1831 | (b) in a case within subsection (2)(b) or (c), when the residual beneficiary becomes entitled to require the trustee to transfer to him any of the property receivable pursuant to the right.
@ref s 139(4) When a residual interest vests in possession (src:1829-1831)
GIVEN case IS A `s 139(4) case of a residual interest`
      `the event mentioned in s 139(2)(a) has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the residual beneficiary has become entitled to require the trustee to transfer to him any of the property receivable pursuant to the right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(4) the residual interest vests in possession` MEANS
    CONSIDER case
    WHEN `s 139(4)(a) a case within subsection (2)(a)` THEN
        IF `the event mentioned in s 139(2)(a) has occurred`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case within subsection (2)(a), on the occurrence of the event mentioned there (whether or not the amount of the property receivable pursuant to the right is ascertained)" ("on" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    WHEN `s 139(4)(b) a case within subsection (2)(b) or (c)` THEN
        IF `the residual beneficiary has become entitled to require the trustee to transfer to him any of the property receivable pursuant to the right`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case within subsection (2)(b) or (c), when the residual beneficiary becomes entitled to require the trustee to transfer to him any of the property receivable pursuant to the right" ("when" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))

-- src:1834 | (a) “relevant benefits” means any pension, lump sum, gratuity or other like benefit given or to be given on retirement or on death or in anticipation of retirement or, in connection with past service, after retirement or death; and
@ref s 139(6)(a) "relevant benefits" (src:1834)
GIVEN `the benefit is a pension, lump sum, gratuity or other like benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is given or to be given on retirement or on death or in anticipation of retirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is given or to be given in connection with past service, after retirement or death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(6)(a) the benefit is a relevant benefit` MEANS
    IF `the benefit is a pension, lump sum, gratuity or other like benefit` AND (`it is given or to be given on retirement or on death or in anticipation of retirement` OR `it is given or to be given in connection with past service, after retirement or death`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant benefits” means any pension, lump sum, gratuity or other like benefit given or to be given on retirement or on death or in anticipation of retirement or, in connection with past service, after retirement or death"

-- src:1835 | (b) “employee” shall be read as if a director of a company were employed by it.
@ref s 139(6)(b) "employee" is read as if a director were employed (src:1835)
GIVEN `the person is employed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139(6)(b) the person is an employee for the purposes of s 139` MEANS
    IF `the person is employed by the company` OR `the person is a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "“employee” shall be read as if a director of a company were employed by it" says what a director is; it does not define "employee" for anyone else

-- src:1836 | 140 Interests to be disregarded: employer's rights of recovery under pension scheme or employees' share scheme
-- src:1837 | (1) Where shares in a company are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme, there shall be disregarded for the purposes of section 138 any charge or lien on, or set-off against, any benefit or other right or interest under the scheme for the purpose of enabling the employer or former employer of a member of the scheme to obtain the discharge of a monetary obligation due to him from the member.
-- src:1838 | (2) In the case of a trust for the purposes of a pension scheme there shall also be disregarded any right to receive from the trustee of the scheme, or as trustee of the scheme to retain, an amount that can be recovered or retained, under ... section 57 of the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993 (c. 49) (deduction of contributions equivalent premium from refund of scheme contributions) or otherwise, as reimbursement or partial reimbursement for any contributions equivalent premium paid in connection with the scheme under Part 3 of that Act.
@ref s 140(1) A charge, lien or set-off to discharge an employer's monetary obligation is disregarded (src:1836-1838)
GIVEN `s 139(1) the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the interest is a charge or lien on, or set-off against, a benefit or other right or interest under the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of enabling the employer or former employer of a member of the scheme to obtain the discharge of a monetary obligation due to him from the member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140 the interest is disregarded for the purposes of s 138` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 139(1) the shares are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares in a company are held on trust for the purposes of a pension scheme or employees' share scheme"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1166 decides "employees' share scheme"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the interest is a charge or lien on, or set-off against, a benefit or other right or interest under the scheme` AND `it is for the purpose of enabling the employer or former employer of a member of the scheme to obtain the discharge of a monetary obligation due to him from the member`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any charge or lien on, or set-off against, any benefit or other right or interest under the scheme for the purpose of enabling the employer or former employer of a member of the scheme to obtain the discharge of a monetary obligation due to him from the member"

-- src:1838 | (2) In the case of a trust for the purposes of a pension scheme there shall also be disregarded any right to receive from the trustee of the scheme, or as trustee of the scheme to retain, an amount that can be recovered or retained, under ... section 57 of the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993 (c. 49) (deduction of contributions equivalent premium from refund of scheme contributions) or otherwise, as reimbursement or partial reimbursement for any contributions equivalent premium paid in connection with the scheme under Part 3 of that Act.
@ref s 140(2) A right to reimbursement for a contributions equivalent premium is also disregarded (src:1838)
GIVEN `the trust is for the purposes of a pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is a right to receive from the trustee of the scheme, or as trustee to retain, an amount that can be recovered or retained as reimbursement for a contributions equivalent premium paid in connection with the scheme under Part 3 of the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(2) the right is also disregarded for the purposes of s 138` MEANS
    IF NOT `the trust is for the purposes of a pension scheme`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a trust for the purposes of a pension scheme there shall also be disregarded"
    ELSE IF `the right is a right to receive from the trustee of the scheme, or as trustee to retain, an amount that can be recovered or retained as reimbursement for a contributions equivalent premium paid in connection with the scheme under Part 3 of the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any right to receive from the trustee of the scheme, or as trustee of the scheme to retain, an amount that can be recovered or retained, under ... section 57 of the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993 ... or otherwise, as reimbursement or partial reimbursement for any contributions equivalent premium"

-- src:1839 | (3) In this section “pension scheme” means a scheme for the provision of benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits for or in respect of employees or former employees.
@ref s 140(3) "pension scheme" (in s 140) (src:1839)
GIVEN `the scheme provides benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits for or in respect of employees or former employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(3) the scheme is a pension scheme` MEANS
    IF `the scheme provides benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits for or in respect of employees or former employees`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “pension scheme” means a scheme for the provision of benefits consisting of or including relevant benefits for or in respect of employees or former employees"

-- src:1840 | “Relevant benefits” here means any pension, lump sum, gratuity or other like benefit given or to be given on retirement or on death or in anticipation of retirement or, in connection with past service, after retirement or death.
@ref s 140(3) "relevant benefits" (in s 140) (src:1840)
GIVEN `the benefit is a pension, lump sum, gratuity or other like benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is given or to be given on retirement or on death or in anticipation of retirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is given or to be given in connection with past service, after retirement or death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(3) the benefit is a relevant benefit` MEANS
    IF `the benefit is a pension, lump sum, gratuity or other like benefit` AND (`it is given or to be given on retirement or on death or in anticipation of retirement` OR `it is given or to be given in connection with past service, after retirement or death`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Relevant benefits” here means any pension, lump sum, gratuity or other like benefit given or to be given on retirement or on death or in anticipation of retirement or, in connection with past service, after retirement or death"

-- src:1841 | (4) In this section “employer” and “employee” shall be read as if a director of a company were employed by it.
@ref s 140(4) "employer" and "employee" are read as if a director were employed (src:1841)
GIVEN `the person is employed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140(4) the person is an employee for the purposes of s 140, and the company is the employer` MEANS
    IF `the person is employed by the company` OR `the person is a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "“employer” and “employee” shall be read as if a director of a company were employed by it" says what a director is; it does not define either word for anyone else

-- ---- s 141: subsidiary acting as authorised dealer in securities -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1843 | 141 Subsidiary acting as authorised dealer in securities
-- src:1844 | (1) The prohibition in section 136 (prohibition on subsidiary being a member of its holding company) does not apply where the shares are held by the subsidiary in the ordinary course of its business as an intermediary.
@ref s 141(1) The prohibition does not apply to shares held in the ordinary course of business as an intermediary (src:1843-1844)
GIVEN `the shares are held by the subsidiary in the ordinary course of its business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 141(2) the subsidiary is an intermediary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(1) the prohibition in section 136 does not apply to the subsidiary` MEANS
    IF NOT `the shares are held by the subsidiary in the ordinary course of its business`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply where the shares are held by the subsidiary in the ordinary course of its business as an intermediary"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 141(2) the subsidiary is an intermediary`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the ordinary course of its business as an intermediary"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 141(2) depends on a UK regulated market (s 1173(1))

-- The five excluded businesses of s 141(3), one fact per limb. Limb (b) turns on "connected" (s 1122 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010,
-- s 141(4)(a)): the person states whether the persons served are connected with the person carrying on the business.
-- src:1849 | (3) The following are excluded businesses—
-- src:1850 | (a) a business that consists wholly or mainly in the making or managing of investments;
-- src:1851 | (b) a business that consists wholly or mainly in, or is carried on wholly or mainly for the purposes of, providing services to persons who are connected with the person carrying on the business;
-- src:1852 | (c) a business that consists in insurance business;
-- src:1853 | (d) a business that consists in managing or acting as trustee in relation to a pension scheme, or that is carried on by the manager or trustee of such a scheme in connection with or for the purposes of the scheme;
-- src:1854 | (e) a business that consists in operating or acting as trustee in relation to a collective investment scheme, or that is carried on by the operator or trustee of such a scheme in connection with and for the purposes of the scheme.
@ref s 141(3) The excluded businesses (src:1849-1854)
DECLARE `s 141(3) business facts` HAS
    `s 141(3)(a) the business consists wholly or mainly in the making or managing of investments` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 141(3)(b) the business consists wholly or mainly in, or is carried on wholly or mainly for the purposes of, providing services to persons connected with the person carrying on the business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 141(3)(c) the business consists in insurance business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 141(3)(d) the business consists in managing or acting as trustee in relation to a pension scheme, or is carried on by the manager or trustee of such a scheme in connection with or for the purposes of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 141(3)(e) the business consists in operating or acting as trustee in relation to a collective investment scheme, or is carried on by the operator or trustee of such a scheme in connection with and for the purposes of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 141(3) The excluded businesses (src:1849-1854)
GIVEN business IS A `s 141(3) business facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(3) the business is an excluded business` MEANS
    IF       business's `s 141(3)(a) the business consists wholly or mainly in the making or managing of investments`
         OR  business's `s 141(3)(b) the business consists wholly or mainly in, or is carried on wholly or mainly for the purposes of, providing services to persons connected with the person carrying on the business`
         OR  business's `s 141(3)(c) the business consists in insurance business`
         OR  business's `s 141(3)(d) the business consists in managing or acting as trustee in relation to a pension scheme, or is carried on by the manager or trustee of such a scheme in connection with or for the purposes of the scheme`
         OR  business's `s 141(3)(e) the business consists in operating or acting as trustee in relation to a collective investment scheme, or is carried on by the operator or trustee of such a scheme in connection with and for the purposes of the scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following are excluded businesses— (a) ... (e)" (read as the definition of "excluded business" that s 141(2)(c) uses, like s 113A(1); fork F16)

-- src:1845 | (2) For this purpose a person is an intermediary if he—
-- src:1846 | (a) carries on a bona fide business of dealing in securities,
-- src:1847 | (b) is a member of or has access to a UK regulated market, and
-- src:1848 | (c) does not carry on an excluded business.
@ref s 141(2) An intermediary (src:1845-1848)
GIVEN `the person carries on a bona fide business of dealing in securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the person is a member of or has access to a UK regulated market` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 141(3) the person carries on an excluded business` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(2) the person is an intermediary` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person carries on a bona fide business of dealing in securities`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is an intermediary if he— (a) carries on a bona fide business of dealing in securities"
    ELSE IF `s 1173(1) the person is a member of or has access to a UK regulated market` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) is a member of or has access to a UK regulated market"
         ELSE IF `s 141(3) the person carries on an excluded business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) does not carry on an excluded business"
              ELSE IF `s 1173(1) the person is a member of or has access to a UK regulated market` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 141(3) the person carries on an excluded business` EQUALS NOTHING
                   THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "UK regulated market" is defined by s 1173(1) and Article 2.1.13A of Regulation (EU) No 600/2014; "excluded business" is a list that is not closed
                   ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1855 | (4) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:1856 | (a) the question whether a person is connected with another shall be determined in accordance with section 1122 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010;
@ref s 141(4)(a) "connected" is decided under section 1122 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010 (src:1855-1856)
GIVEN `s 1122 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010 the person is connected with the other person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(4)(a) the person is connected with the other person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1122 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010 the person is connected with the other person`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the question whether a person is connected with another shall be determined in accordance with section 1122 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010" (the answer is that section's)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1122 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010 is not among the sources

-- src:1855 | (4) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:1857 | (b) “collective investment scheme” has the meaning given in section 235 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8);
@ref s 141(4)(b) "collective investment scheme" has the meaning given in section 235 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (src:1855 and src:1857)
GIVEN `s 235 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 the arrangement is a collective investment scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(4)(b) the arrangement is a collective investment scheme` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 235 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 the arrangement is a collective investment scheme`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“collective investment scheme” has the meaning given in section 235 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000" (the answer is that section's)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 235 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 is not among the sources

-- src:1855 | (4) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:1858 | (c) “insurance business” means business that consists in the effecting or carrying out of contracts of insurance;
@ref s 141(4)(c) "insurance business" (src:1855 and src:1858)
GIVEN `the business consists in the effecting or carrying out of contracts of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(4)(c) the business is insurance business` MEANS
    IF `the business consists in the effecting or carrying out of contracts of insurance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“insurance business” means business that consists in the effecting or carrying out of contracts of insurance"

DECLARE `s 141(4)(d) kind of investment` IS ONE OF
    `s 141(4)(d)(i) options`
    `s 141(4)(d)(ii) futures`
    `s 141(4)(d)(iii) contracts for differences`
    `s 141(4)(d) rights or interests in those investments`
    `s 141(4)(d) another investment`

-- src:1855 | (4) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:1859 | (d) “securities” includes—
-- src:1860 | (i) options,
-- src:1861 | (ii) futures, and
-- src:1862 | (iii) contracts for differences,
-- src:1863 | and rights or interests in those investments;
@ref s 141(4)(d) "securities" includes (src:1855 and src:1859-1863)
GIVEN investment IS A `s 141(4)(d) kind of investment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(4)(d) the investment is within "securities"` MEANS
    CONSIDER investment
    WHEN `s 141(4)(d)(i) options` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 141(4)(d)(ii) futures` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 141(4)(d)(iii) contracts for differences` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 141(4)(d) rights or interests in those investments` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 141(4)(d) another investment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“securities” includes— (i) options, (ii) futures, and (iii) contracts for differences, and rights or interests in those investments" (an inclusive definition says nothing of other investments)

-- src:1855 | (4) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:1864 | (e) “trustee” and “the operator” in relation to a collective investment scheme shall be construed in accordance with section 237(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8).
@ref s 141(4)(e) "trustee" and "the operator" are construed in accordance with section 237(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (src:1855 and src:1864)
GIVEN `s 237(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 the person is the trustee or the operator of the collective investment scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(4)(e) the person is the trustee or the operator of the collective investment scheme` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 237(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 the person is the trustee or the operator of the collective investment scheme`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“trustee” and “the operator” in relation to a collective investment scheme shall be construed in accordance with section 237(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000" (the answer is that section's)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 237(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 is not among the sources

-- src:1865 | (5) Expressions used in this section that are also used in the provisions regulating activities under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 have the same meaning here as they do in those provisions.
-- src:1866 | See section 22 of that Act, orders made under that section and Schedule 2 to that Act.
@ref s 141(5) Expressions that are also used in the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (src:1865-1866)
GIVEN `the expression is also used in the provisions regulating activities under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(5) the expression has the same meaning here as in those provisions` MEANS
    IF `the expression is also used in the provisions regulating activities under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Expressions used in this section that are also used in the provisions regulating activities under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000"

-- ---- s 142: protection of third parties ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1867 | 142 Protection of third parties in other cases where subsidiary acting as dealer in securities
-- src:1868 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:1869 | (a) a subsidiary that is a dealer in securities has purportedly acquired shares in its holding company in contravention of the prohibition in section 136, and
-- src:1870 | (b) a person acting in good faith has agreed, for value and without notice of the contravention, to acquire shares in the holding company—
-- src:1871 | (i) from the subsidiary, or
-- src:1872 | (ii) from someone who has purportedly acquired the shares after their disposal by the subsidiary.
@ref s 142(1) Where the section applies (src:1867-1872)
GIVEN `a subsidiary that is a dealer in securities has purportedly acquired shares in its holding company in contravention of the prohibition in section 136` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person acting in good faith has agreed to acquire shares in the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is for value and without notice of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are acquired from the subsidiary, or from someone who has purportedly acquired the shares after their disposal by the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 142(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF       `a subsidiary that is a dealer in securities has purportedly acquired shares in its holding company in contravention of the prohibition in section 136`
         AND `a person acting in good faith has agreed to acquire shares in the holding company`
         AND `the agreement is for value and without notice of the contravention`
         AND `the shares are acquired from the subsidiary, or from someone who has purportedly acquired the shares after their disposal by the subsidiary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where (a) a subsidiary that is a dealer in securities has purportedly acquired shares in its holding company in contravention of the prohibition in section 136, and (b) a person acting in good faith has agreed, for value and without notice of the contravention, to acquire shares in the holding company"

-- src:1873 | (2) A transfer to that person of the shares mentioned in subsection (1)(a) has the same effect as it would have had if their original acquisition by the subsidiary had not been in contravention of the prohibition.
@ref s 142(2) A transfer to that person has the same effect as if the acquisition had not been in contravention (src:1873)
GIVEN `s 142(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 142(2) the transfer to that person has the same effect as it would have had if the original acquisition by the subsidiary had not been in contravention` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 142(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" (s 142(1))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer of s 142(1) is not known

-- ---- ss 143 and 144: supplementary --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1875 | 143 Application of provisions to companies not limited by shares
-- src:1876 | In relation to a company other than a company limited by shares, the references in this Chapter to shares shall be read as references to the interest of its members as such, whatever the form of that interest.
@ref s 143 Application of provisions to companies not limited by shares (src:1875-1876)
GIVEN `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 143 the references in this Chapter to shares are read as references to the interest of its members as such, whatever the form of that interest` MEANS
    IF `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a company other than a company limited by shares"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1877 | 144 Application of provisions to nominees
-- src:1878 | The provisions of this Chapter apply to a nominee acting on behalf of a subsidiary as to the subsidiary itself.
@ref s 144 Application of provisions to nominees (src:1877-1878)
GIVEN `the person is a nominee acting on behalf of a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144 the provisions of this Chapter apply to the nominee as to the subsidiary itself` MEANS
    IF `the person is a nominee acting on behalf of a subsidiary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a nominee acting on behalf of a subsidiary"
